<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicolás Avellaneda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1885</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicolás Avellaneda was an Argentine lawyer and statesman who served as president from 1874 to 1880. Earlier Sarmiento's minister of education, he continued the expansion of schools, encouraged immigration and backed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conquest-of-the-desert">Conquest of the Desert</a> against the Indigenous peoples of the south. At the end of his term <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> was federalised as the national capital in 1880.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicolas-avellaneda.jpg" alt="Nicolás Avellaneda" width="320" height="447" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicol%C3%A1s_Avellaneda_-_1910.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
